# The repo is a product and a website in one tree. Only the website should be
# published to the marketing domain — the source stays on GitHub, where people
# expect to read it, rather than being served from costgrid.org.
node_modules
packages
# The product scripts stay off the site. The install helper is the exception:
# vercel.json can only point at it, because installCommand is capped at 256 characters.
scripts/**
!scripts/vercel-install.sh
docs
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.env.example
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.base.json
vitest.config.ts
# Only the product package files. api/package.json is the function install.
/package.json
/package-lock.json
*.db
# Unit tests are not part of the site. The billing functions import site/stripe,
# so that directory is deployed and redirected away from the public site.
test
# Repository files that are not part of the site. Nothing here is secret, but
# with the code repository private they should not be reachable by address.
README.md
design-system
supabase
